{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/927711-what-to-do-when-they-are-not-there","id":927711,"title":"What to do when they are not there??!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-07T11:37:38-07:00","id":927711,"title":"What to do when they are not there??!","content":"OK, brought out of the thread on &quot;What to not do as a VtM ST..&quot;<br /> <br /> What do YOU do as a ST/DM/GM when a player of a character in your group is not going to be there (Or leaves early for what ever reason)?<br /> <br /> Do you take over his character?<br /> Does he get played by another player?<br /> Does he just 'poof' out of existence?<br /> <br /> If he's still getting played, can bad things (damage, potential death, dominated, bloodbonded etc) happen? Or is he somehow plot immune to all of them while being played by someone else?<br /> Does his Character still earn full XP that everyone else gets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:07:03-07:00","id":927722,"title":"","content":"Depends on when my group left off, if it's in say the middle of an important combat I'll just roll the dice myself. <br /> If it's not really important they get some call from an npc (plot hook related) that takes them out of play for the session. <br /> <br /> My group is pretty adult about pc loss so if something happens and it made sense as to why it happened then it's all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:38:43-07:00","id":928110,"title":"","content":"Somethings can easily avoided with good communication. Unless it's an emergency nobody involved leaves mid-scene. If a player or the st are getting tired, they should tell in advance. <br /> If a player can't make it to the appointment, he will go puff with a good ingame explanation, XP are rewarded if it's happens seldom, if she/he misses every second or so appointment he/she will not get the XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:18:10-07:00","id":928286,"title":"","content":"Also, make sure to talk with your players in advance about stuff like this. This sets expectations and might prevent unnecessary drama in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:36:14-07:00","id":928435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/927711-what-to-do-when-they-are-not-there?p=928286#post928286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, make sure to talk with your players in advance about stuff like this. This sets expectations and might prevent unnecessary drama in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have heard people say that elsewhere. One of the &quot;House&quot; rules, (like who buys food, what rotation is done for drinks etc) was &quot;What happens to characters if player(s) can't make it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}